<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine utility sale draw 14 qualified bidders.</title>
<headline>Argentine utility sale draw 14 qualified bidders.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fourteen international consortiums have qualified to bid in the privatization of Buenos Aires province's electric utility Eseba, the government of Buenos Aires said Monday.</p>
<p>Bidders included Chilean companies Chilquinta SA, Enersis SA and Chilectra SA.</p>
<p>Houston Argentina SA is bidding jointly with Argentina's Techint. CMS Energy Corp of the United States, CEA Operating Argentina and Camuzzi SA were other bidders.</p>
<p>Argentine energy distributors Edenor and Edesur, Argentina's Grupo Cartellone, AES Development of Argentina and Spain's Iberdrola were also bidding.</p>
<p>Other bidders were electricity generator Central Costanera, and Ontario Hydro International.</p>
<p>Buenos Aires Gov. Eduardo Duhalde has said he hopes to raise $1 billion by the sale of Eseba.</p>
<p>((--Guillermo Haskel, Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0650))</p>
